1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,200
Isasumi, Chilchuk?

2
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,960
Do you mind slowing down a bit?

3
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:14,660
The floor is full of gaps and it's hard to walk on.

4
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,260
I didn't even notice.

5
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:19,700
Let's take a little break.

6
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:23,140
Sure, whatever you say, Grandpa.

7
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:25,840
There's something I've been wondering.

8
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,640
In these bodies,

9
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:31,300
what's the gap between our actual age and the age we look?

10
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:33,820
Laios, how old are you?

11
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,860
I'm 26 years old.

12
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:37,540
Senshi, now that he's a dwarf,

13
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,340
how old does Laios look to you?

14
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:42,140
Hmm, I would say around 60.

15
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:45,520
Dwarves live about two and a half times longer than tall men.

16
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:48,400
So if I'm 26 as a tall man,

17
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,140
I'd be 65 as a dwarf.

18
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:54,680
If our appearance adjusts our age relative to what race we are,

19
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:57,780
I'm kind of worried about our remaining lifespan.

20
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:00,980
Will we age at the rate we did before we transformed?

21
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,660
Or will that change based on our new bodies?

22
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:05,660
Hey, Marcel,

23
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,080
if you think that doesn't affect you, you're wrong.

24
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,580
Since you're a half foot now,

25
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,740
if it's the latter,

26
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,120
you'll only live till about 50 years old.

27
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,760
In less than 40 years,

28
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:17,300
you're gonna get all old and wrinkly and then die.

29
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:23,440
A half foot's lifespan is that short?

30
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:24,740
I thought they lived to 100.

31
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:27,280
There are some who live that long.

32
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,720
But it's pretty rare.

33
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:35,600
I'm only kidding.

34
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:38,200
What I'm actually trying to say is,

35
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:39,300
if that was the case,

36
00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:41,200
then this mushroom is too good to be true.

37
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,840
There are tons of people out there

38
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:45,020
who would pay a fortune to become another race,

39
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:47,500
but I've never seen this mushroom in the markets.

40
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:49,740
It means the change is only temporary

41
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:52,420
or has some kind of awful side effect.

42
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:54,220
Side effects, huh?

43
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:55,680
Possibly.

44
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:58,720
I thought about using the changelings for something,

45
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,360
but I don't think it'd go well.

46
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:01,780
What kind of something?

47
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:04,000
You want to be a demi-human, don't you?

48
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,300
No, that's not it.

49
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:08,640
I was honestly thinking more in regards to Fallon.

50
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:09,840
What about her?

51
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:11,820
Now, this is all hypothetical,

52
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:14,040
but what if everything worked out

53
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,600
and we defeated the Mad Mage?

54
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:17,620
I've learned my lesson.

55
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:19,500
Fallon regains her sanity.

56
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:20,120
Huh?

57
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:22,200
What was I just doing?

58
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:23,340
Fallon's back!

59
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,320
We return to the surface.

60
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:27,300
Man, that was really rough, wasn't it?

61
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:29,700
She scares people.

62
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,620
So, in that case,

63
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:34,920
having a dragon's lower half would be a problem.

64
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,100
Hold on.

65
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:37,820
Let's hear what he has to say.

66
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:41,180
I thought about hiding that part by putting her in a hole.

67
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,340
What can I get to?

68
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:42,940
However,

69
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:46,320
a large monster can't survive in a human town

70
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:47,680
with how thin the mana is.

71
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,060
Like how a fish can't survive outside of water,

72
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:54,420
Fallon might not be able to live among humans anymore.

73
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,040
Unless...

74
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,160
We use those mushrooms.

75
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,840
With the changelings,

76
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,760
we could change her lower half

77
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,140
into another type of dragon

78
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:04,100
that's smaller.

79
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,480
And that way,

80
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:08,080
Fallon could live in town after all!

81
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,160
What?

82
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,260
He's so stupidly optimistic.

83
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:11,860
Miss!

84
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:12,440
Miss!

85
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:13,280
Though,

86
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:16,480
I won't deny wanting to change into something else, too.

87
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,920
Tall men don't have any kind of special trait,

88
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,080
which makes us plain.

89
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:20,820
Jilchuk,

90
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:22,680
do you hear something strange?

91
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:23,640
Oh, uh,

92
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:25,900
do you think it's the dwarven relic or something?

93
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:26,900
No,

94
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,660
it's like stones scraping against each other.

95
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,380
From what I can tell,

96
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:33,380
it actually sounds like it's getting closer.

97
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:36,640
This is bad!

98
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,820
The gargoyles found us!

99
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,100
You idiot!

100
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,980
Did you really not shut the door all the way?

101
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:44,180
We need to hurry and get out of here

102
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:46,080
before they catch up to us!

103
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,600
They're just gonna keep chasing us

104
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:49,500
unless we do something.

105
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,220
Let's set up an ambush and take them down.

106
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,640
But, Laios...

107
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:55,620
I'll draw them to me.

108
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:56,540
Jilchuk,

109
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,300
get the pan!

110
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,040
Izutsumi,

111
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:58,940
attack from behind!

112
00:03:59,420 --> 00:03:59,760
Senji,

113
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:00,580
wait for an opening.

114
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:01,240
Marcel,

115
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,300
where are they?

116
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:03,560
I told you!

117
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,160
They're right there!

118
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:08,940
Laios!

119
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:12,220
Dammit!

120
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:14,120
Watch out, everyone!

121
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:21,740
Now do you understand

122
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:22,840
why I quickly run off

123
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,000
and find a place to hide?

124
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,980
Don't stand around people's legs!

125
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:27,280
You say that, but...

126
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:29,720
You're clumsy no matter what body you're in, huh?

127
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:30,680
This way!

128
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:36,660
Where did this smoke come from?

129
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:39,020
Did you cast something?

130
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,120
Are you two hurt?

131
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,520
No, we're fine.

132
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:44,080
It went right between our arms.

133
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:44,940
Good.

134
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:47,120
You mind grabbing Kensuke for me?

135
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:47,500
Sure.

136
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:52,680
Has it always looked like this?

137
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:53,280
No.

138
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:55,520
How and when did it change, then?

139
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:58,100
You think that maybe the smoke we saw

140
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:00,740
was actually changeling spores?

141
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:02,360
But, hang on.

142
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:04,980
There wasn't a mushroom ring anywhere near here.

143
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:07,320
Our arms were a ring when it passed through them.

144
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:10,500
Wait, so that means...

145
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:18,480
Quit buzzing around, dammit!

146
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:19,520
You guys!

147
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:20,820
Grab each other's hands

148
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,300
and make a circle right now!

149
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,140
Think before you open your mouth for once!

150
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:25,120
Just trust me, okay?

151
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:28,820
Well?

152
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,360
What do we do now?

153
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:31,160
Is this it?

154
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,700
We're gonna have the gargoyle

155
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:33,800
pass through our arms.

156
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:35,480
If my theory is correct,

157
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,620
then the gargoyle

158
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:38,300
should change into something else!

159
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:41,280
All right, it's time!

160
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,000
The wall's in that direction!

161
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:43,880
Come this way!

162
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:44,200
Hey!

163
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:44,960
Stop!

164
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,020
You're hurting me!

165
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:51,980
Oh, no!

166
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:04,820
It can't fly away anymore!

167
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:05,460
Come on!

168
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:06,420
Let's surround it!

169
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:16,480
We did it!

170
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:17,720
Where'd it go?

171
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:18,800
Look!

172
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:23,740
This is the gargoyle?

173
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,580
It really did change.

174
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:26,860
I see.

175
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,340
It works like this, too.

176
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:29,880
So non-living,

177
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,380
things transform faster!

178
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:33,100
Glyos!

179
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:34,100
Are you okay?

180
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,460
My head hurts,

181
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:36,260
but I'm fine.

182
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:37,660
Dwarves' bodies

183
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:38,960
are as tough as they say.

184
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:43,400
Doesn't seem like

185
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,600
it's gonna come down here.

186
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:45,920
How are we supposed

187
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:46,800
to get it to pass

188
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,660
through our arms?

189
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:52,860
Marcil?

190
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:53,400
Yeah?

191
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:54,380
What if we...

192
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:59,420
It should work.

193
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:00,060
What should...

194
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:00,720
Let's do it!

195
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,180
Right.

196
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,040
We're gonna bring

197
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,380
ourselves closer to it

198
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:06,320
and get it to attack us!

199
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,120
Keep in rhythm

200
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,340
so we run and sink!

201
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:09,460
Let's go!

202
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:10,560
One!

203
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,560
Two!

204
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,000
One!

205
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:12,560
Two!

206
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:12,800
One!

207
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:13,700
Two!

208
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:14,500
One!

209
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:14,800
One!

210
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:15,720
Two!

211
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:17,940
One and two and one

212
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:19,180
and two and one

213
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:20,180
and two and...

214
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:23,280
It's making its move!

215
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:24,360
You ready to do this?

216
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:24,780
Ready!

217
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:26,000
Ready for what?

218
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,680
Ready and...

219
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:29,080
Take to the sky, Marcil!

220
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:29,360
Marcil!

221
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,080
Ah!

222
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:45,660
Good riddance.

223
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,840
It's kind of anticlimactic,

224
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,400
but if you wash off

225
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,960
the spores stuck to your body,

226
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:53,220
you'll go back to normal.

227
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,480
Can you please not?

228
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:56,580
All it is is water,

229
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,340
so it's fine.

230
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:58,920
Gotta rinse the spores

231
00:07:58,920 --> 00:07:59,540
off thoroughly.

232
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:00,800
We're basically

233
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,200
the mushroom seedbed

234
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:02,720
right now.

235
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:05,680
I think I finally understand

236
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:06,560
why the mushrooms

237
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,880
behave the way they do.

238
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:10,120
An animal steps

239
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,240
into a changeling ring

240
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,280
and transforms.

241
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:14,080
They get shunned

242
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:14,900
by their kind,

243
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:16,300
then they die,

244
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:17,320
and eventually

245
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,360
become new changelings.

246
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:20,400
What an awful

247
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,220
side effect.

248
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:23,320
Since we're not gargoyles,

249
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,460
it's gonna take some time

250
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:25,760
to go back to how we were.

251
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:27,040
Why don't we prepare

252
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,180
a meal while we wait?

253
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:30,200
Very well.

254
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:34,140
Kensuke,

255
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:35,820
it's hard to believe

256
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:37,240
that this is you now.

257
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,920
Maybe it's a bit of a stretch

258
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:40,880
to think the mushrooms

259
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:42,060
were the cause of this.

260
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:44,120
Will washing you

261
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,160
change you back?

262
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,420
What's on the menu?

263
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,500
We have some leftover dumplings,

264
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:52,880
so I'll be boiling those.

265
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:53,660
Really?

266
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:54,260
Again?

267
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,220
Is there a problem with that?

268
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:57,200
Nah,

269
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:58,620
I'm just kind of sick of them.

270
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:00,500
Sick of them?

271
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:01,960
Wish I could be that carefree.

272
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:05,580
Let's cook them another way.

273
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,880
Heat some oil in a frying pan,

274
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:11,040
then gently put the dumplings in.

275
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:13,220
Oh, shit.

276
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:15,340
When golden brown,

277
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:16,440
remove the dumplings

278
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:18,060
and blot the excess oil.

279
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:19,800
On top of Izutsumi

280
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,020
having a small appetite,

281
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:22,360
she won't eat anything

282
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,240
she doesn't like.

283
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:24,800
So it's important

284
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,160
I take extra care

285
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,180
to make sure

286
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:28,220
she eats her fill.

287
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,160
Tell me,

288
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:33,320
what do you think?

289
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:34,980
You just fried them.

290
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:37,020
Could you not?

291
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:38,240
Huh?

292
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,240
What if...

293
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:50,840
Oh, it changed its shape.

